\citation{Voronov}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Theorem\nonbreakingspace \ref  {thm:law} as a sieve, over the integer spindles $a \le 100$. Top: the $59$ \emph  {positive} squared radii at which $R$ has points, decided by the form \textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {eq:norm}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}} rather than by a ball, and in closed form by Theorem\nonbreakingspace \ref  {prop:shells}. Middle: the multiples of $4$. Bottom: their intersection, the sixteen multiples of $4$ with an \emph  {occupied} shell---the candidates, in the sense Section\nonbreakingspace \ref  {sec:seven} fixes. The nine gaps there are the multiples of $4$ whose shell is empty, $a = 8$, $24$, $32$, $40$, $56$, $68$, $72$, $88$, $96$; they lie outside this accounting altogether, because at an empty shell Theorem\nonbreakingspace \ref  {thm:law} is silent in both directions. The law is a kill, not a construction, so the bottom row also carries what became of each candidate: filled, the four given a verified 5-chromatic union in Section\nonbreakingspace \ref  {sec:seven}; grey, the eleven the stronger filter of Section\nonbreakingspace \ref  {sec:stronger} kills; open, $a = 64$, on which that filter degenerates at every modulus tried---it joins all the same, by Lemma\nonbreakingspace \ref  {lem:chain}, which builds a graph there rather than testing one.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:law}{{2}{5}{Theorem~\ref {thm:law} as a sieve, over the integer spindles $a \le 100$. Top: the $59$ \emph {positive} squared radii at which $\Lat $ has points, decided by the form \eqref {eq:norm} rather than by a ball, and in closed form by Theorem~\ref {prop:shells}. Middle: the multiples of $4$. Bottom: their intersection, the sixteen multiples of $4$ with an \emph {occupied} shell---the candidates, in the sense Section~\ref {sec:seven} fixes. The nine gaps there are the multiples of $4$ whose shell is empty, $a = 8$, $24$, $32$, $40$, $56$, $68$, $72$, $88$, $96$; they lie outside this accounting altogether, because at an empty shell Theorem~\ref {thm:law} is silent in both directions. The law is a kill, not a construction, so the bottom row also carries what became of each candidate: filled, the four given a verified 5-chromatic union in Section~\ref {sec:seven}; grey, the eleven the stronger filter of Section~\ref {sec:stronger} kills; open, $a = 64$, on which that filter degenerates at every modulus tried---it joins all the same, by Lemma~\ref {lem:chain}, which builds a graph there rather than testing one}{figure.2}{}}
\citation{Voronov}
